# Shell scripts and systemd units are executed on Linux. Git on Windows checks files out with
# CRLF by default, and a CRLF shebang line makes bash fail with the famously unhelpful
# "$'\r': command not found" -- which is exactly what happened when deploy/pi/setup.sh was
# copied from a Windows checkout to a Raspberry Pi. Pin these to LF everywhere.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.service   text eol=lf
*.bash      text eol=lf

# Captured wire responses used as connector fixtures. These are evidence of what a host
# actually sent, and their bytes are content-hashed, so no end-of-line conversion may touch
# them on checkout.
tests/fixtures/arxiv_*   -text
